  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x201c;Mamuncia&#x201d; Program for the Cauca Littoral</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program contributes to the inclusion and improvement of quality of life of ethnic communities in the Cauca coastline of Colombia, through an intervention model based on the ethnic traditional practice of these territories called &#x201c;Mamuncia&#x201d; and a cross cutting gender strategy. In particular, the program develops co-creation spaces with the participation of Government Institutions, Civil Society Organizations (CSOs) and the education sector to open effective and sustainable dialogue paths toward finding solutions to the problems that have historically afflicted the region, and to generate synergies between the Government of Colombia and CSOs. The co-creation spaces are centered around five lines of work: Organization and Institutional Strengthening, Acceleration of Entrepreneurships, Heritage Protection, Knowledge Transfer (on Gender-Based Violence), and Access and Quality of Education.</narrative>
  </description>
